 "notes": "Hidden-photon (dark-photon) DM search with BRASS-p prototype, mass range 49.63-74.44 ueV (12-18 GHz). Headline curve is the V-polarisation kinetic-mixing detection sensitivity chi(nu) (Fig.11 bottom panel, sensitivitySR1.png raster; V-Pol is the channel used for the Fig.12 comparison, per text). Curve is the median of the noisy per-channel band extracted by pixel calibration (x gridlines 50-75 ueV, y gridlines 5/10/15 x1e-14). chi reported directly (not chi^2). Values ~6.5-11.5 x1e-14, consistent with abstract record sensitivity (0.3-1.0)x1e-13. This is a 1-sigma detection sensitivity from measured cumulative noise power (Eq.3.4, alpha=1/3 single pol); the detailed signal search is deferred to a later publication, so CL=1sigma(~0.68) rather than 90/95%. rho_DM=0.3 GeV/cm^3 (Eq.2.2/3.4). Unpolarised (gas-like) HP scenario assumed.",
